GEOS submodule src/cmake/blt (BLT 0.6.2, 9ff77344f0b2a6ee345e452bddd6bfd46cbbfa35) -- CUDA 13: memoryClockRate

Class: build-system/test-fixture compatibility fix, back-port of upstream BLT
commit 38b46203cf42 ("Set memory clock rate based on the cuda runtime version",
LLNL/blt develop, 2025-09-07); applied to the smoke test only.
Problem: CUDA 13 removed cudaDeviceProp::memoryClockRate; BLT 0.6.2's CUDA
runtime smoke test (built whenever ENABLE_TESTS is on, GEOS' default) fails to
compile with nvcc 13.2 ("'struct cudaDeviceProp' has no member named
'memoryClockRate'"), which stops the GEOS build although nothing in GEOS itself
is affected. Fix: query cudaDevAttrMemoryClockRate through
cudaDeviceGetAttribute when CUDART_VERSION >= 13000, exactly as upstream BLT
does. Impact: none on GEOS (a smoke-test executable). Verified: the target
compiles; GEOS builds with upstream's default ENABLE_TESTS=ON. Applied by
level3/geos/build.sh (git apply in the submodule, idempotent); hash recorded in
the profile fingerprint.

--- a/tests/smoke/blt_cuda_runtime_smoke.cpp
+++ b/tests/smoke/blt_cuda_runtime_smoke.cpp
@@ -27,15 +27,23 @@
   for (int i = 0; i < nDevices; i++)
   {
     cudaDeviceProp prop;
+    int memoryClockRate;
     cudaGetDeviceProperties(&prop, i);
+
+#if CUDART_VERSION >= 13000
+    cudaDeviceGetAttribute(&memoryClockRate, cudaDevAttrMemoryClockRate, i);
+#else
+    memoryClockRate = prop.memoryClockRate;
+#endif
+
     printf("Device Number: %d\n", i);
     printf("  Device name: %s\n", prop.name);
     printf("  Memory Clock Rate (KHz): %d\n",
-           prop.memoryClockRate);
+           memoryClockRate);
     printf("  Memory Bus Width (bits): %d\n",
            prop.memoryBusWidth);
     printf("  Peak Memory Bandwidth (GB/s): %f\n\n",
-           2.0*prop.memoryClockRate*(prop.memoryBusWidth/8)/1.0e6);
+           2.0*memoryClockRate*(prop.memoryBusWidth/8)/1.0e6);
   }
 
   return 0;
